============================================================================================
is cert4.cells(W) EXHAUSTIVE?  --  the analytic bound, with every ingredient checked
============================================================================================

(1) maximum weight of a single residual set  (RES_POS = r1={i1,i2}, r2={i4,i5,i6}, r3={i5,i6})
    sector Z: weights by k = {(0, 2): 72, (1, 3): 72, (2, 2): 72}   -> wmax = 3
    sector X: weights by k = {(0, 2): 72, (1, 3): 72, (2, 2): 72}   -> wmax = 3
    wmax over both sectors = 3      (the bound needs wmax <= 3: True)

(2) parity: is the all-ones vector in rowspace(H_X) and rowspace(H_Z)?
    all-ones in rowspace(H_X): True     in rowspace(H_Z): True
    => every stabiliser coset has constant weight parity, so |E| is EVEN: True
    weight parities actually present in the weight-12 logical pools: {'Z': [0], 'X': [0]}

(3) lower bound |E| >= 12
    the gross code is [[144, 12, 12]]; the pools hold the weight-12 non-trivial logicals
    pool sizes |PZ| = 1884, |PX| = 1884, all of weight 12: True
    corroborated in-session by anchor2/anchor3: with residuals OFF,
      [Z] W = 11 UNSAT, W = 12 SAT     [X] W = 11 UNSAT, W = 12 SAT
    i.e. no non-trivial logical of weight <= 11 exists in either sector.

(4) the two bounds vs. what cells(W) actually enumerates, W = 10
    allowed by the analytic bounds : 55 cells
    cert4.cells(10) returns         : 55 cells
    cells() MISSES an allowed cell : []   <-- must be empty for exhaustiveness
    cells() includes extra cells   : []   (harmless: extra cells are merely decided UNSAT)

============================================================================================
VERDICT: cells(10) is EXHAUSTIVE -- it covers every (K, |E|) a weight-<=10 solution can occupy.
============================================================================================
